      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If you set this property’s value to `1.0`, this interpolator expects that each pixel’s motion vector points to the location where that pixel is in the [`prevColorTexture`](mtlfxframeinterpolatorbase/prevcolortexture.md).",
      "normalizedSource": "If you set this property’s value to `1.0`, this interpolator expects that each pixel’s motion vector points to the location where that pixel is in the [`prevColorTexture`](mtlfxframeinterpolatorbase/prevcolortexture.md).",
      "sourceHash": "30392626f5e04ba88e2ec853e0f61ee207f5ff1e0d64391acb2ee7bb1673da9e",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The frame interpolator converts the horizontal component of each value in [`motionTexture`](mtlfxframeinterpolatorbase/motiontexture.md) into fragment (pixel) coordinates by multiplying it by this property’s value.",
      "contextAfter": "For example, in Metal’s standard device coordinates where `(0,0)` represents the upper-left corner of the framebuffer, the motion vectors for an object that moves down and to the right in the [`colorTexture`](mtlfxframeinterpolatorbase/colortexture.md) by `10` pixels would be `(-10,-10)`.",
